g its line of findings; a `graph` tool call answering its line of the UI graph; an `actions` tool call answering its line of the actionable nodes, an argument to it reading `isError`; protocol errors run nothing and leak nothing; unix only, a snapshot equal through MCP and the command line) and `mcp_log` (the role at `RUST_LOG=trace`: no id, name or typed text, one `tool_call` line per call, under both builds; twelve tool calls and 10 `command` lines, one `lint`, one `snapshot` part read, one `graph` call and one `actions` call among them, 0 graph and 0 actions needles read; since 2026-10-19-session-recording a second test, a recording `mcp` role that logs nothing of its checks; and a third, a select list opened and chosen through the role, `a_select_list_opened_and_chosen_through_the_role_logs_no_option_at_trace`, which records nothing — 0 option needles at `trace`), not unix-gated but the comparison and, since that chunk, every check that records (`mcp_log`'s recorded test, the shared `common::recorded_needles` (its own until 2026-10-19-test-splits), `the_check`) — and in process `stand_mcp_tools` (blitz-tests; the flow through `serve_mcp` in both layout modes, one `tool_call` span the parent of each `command`; since 2026-10-19-visual-lint a `lint` tool call answering the reader's findings and parenting its `command` span; since 2026-11-07-ui-graph a `graph` tool call answering the reader's graph, its `tool_call` span parenting one `command` span that records `verb` alone, and since 2026-11-08-what-can-i-do-here an `actions` tool call answering the reader's nodes the same way, the two through one shared helper; since 2026-10-12-self-description every cause a tool call reaches served with its remedy, `covered` on an overlay fixture, and `help` answered by the server, parenting no `command` span) and, since 2026-10-12-self-description, `stand_mcp_masked` (a password typed through an MCP `type` reads `MASKED_VALUE` and never the typed text, role `PasswordInput` with 